{
  "_meta": {
    "category": "overlays",
    "description": "Compose batch of three crosstab slots on experiment.pulse, one per segment (FILTER_INCLUDE), over region x converted (count cells), decorated with an OVERLAY_PROP_Z_PANEL cell overlay: pooled two-proportion z-tests between every pair of slots in the panel (the reference segment_a and the targets segment_b and segment_c), the cell the successes and the row margin the n. Each overlay cell is the flattened upper triangle of pairwise two-sided p-values, M*(M-1)/2 long for M slots: here (a, b), (a, c), (b, c), so the yes column says which segments convert differently in each region (segment_a against segment_c below 0.01 in three of the four). Each p equals OVERLAY_PROP_Z_CELL's (13_compose_prop_z_cell.json) for the same pair. At most 16 targets by default (PULSE_OVERLAY_PANEL_TARGETS_OVER_CAP). Buffered.",
    "intents": [
      "compare_groups",
      "benchmark"
    ],
    "name": "compose-prop-z-panel",
    "operators": [
      "AGG_COUNT",
      "FILTER_INCLUDE",
      "GROUP_CATEGORY"
    ],
    "tags": [
